WAKE UP SLOW.  (30 s; 1 scenes, 8 shots)
synopsis: At dawn in the Morning Kitchen, hot coffee steams inside a ceramic Plaid Mug resting on a wooden table, its handle toward the edge. Closer views reveal the plaid pattern as a faint birdcall sounds outside. Alex's hand enters, settles around the handle, pauses, then slowly lifts the mug out of view. The camera holds on the empty table as the Cabin Coffee Company logo appears, followed beneath by the words Wake up slow.
theme: Permission to begin gently, without urgency.
music: Minimal ambient acoustic instrumental, warm and patient, sparse felt piano and soft acoustic-guitar harmonics, 60 bpm, no percussion or vocals, very low in the mix.   arc: [0s] Begin almost inaudibly, with widely spaced notes.  [16s] Thin to a nearly silent sustained tone, leaving the scrape exposed.  [24s] Resolve into one warm, restrained chord beneath the brand reveal.  [28s] Let the final resonance fade naturally to the end.

